WEBVTT


00:00:58.675 --> 00:01:00.021
Who's there?!


00:01:02.621 --> 00:01:04.039
Who's there?!


00:01:45.128 --> 00:01:47.195
What do you want?!


00:02:29.557 --> 00:02:32.172
<i>Some say
the world will end in fire.</i>


00:02:33.502 --> 00:02:35.454
<i>Some say in ice...</i>


00:02:36.365 --> 00:02:41.079
From what I've tasted of desire,
I hold with those who favor fire.


00:02:43.158 --> 00:02:46.007
But if I had to perish twice...


00:02:47.753 --> 00:02:50.390
I think I know enough of hate,


00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.587
To say that,
for destruction,


00:02:52.587 --> 00:02:56.980
Ice,
is also great.


00:02:59.076 --> 00:03:00.737
And would suffice.


00:03:01.694 --> 00:03:04.993
You know,
I've got an english final.


00:03:04.993 --> 00:03:07.052
I gotta focus.


00:03:21.484 --> 00:03:23.365
Marry me.


00:03:24.241 --> 00:03:24.991
No.


00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.093
Marry me.


00:03:40.382 --> 00:03:42.053
Change me.


00:03:47.623 --> 00:03:52.120
Okey I will if you marry me,
It's called a compromise.


00:03:56.862 --> 00:03:59.221
It's just called coercion.


00:03:59.221 --> 00:04:01.019
It's not fair.


00:04:02.388 --> 00:04:04.558
Marriage is just...


00:04:04.558 --> 00:04:06.995
Is a piece of paper.


00:04:08.733 --> 00:04:11.985
Where I am from,
it's the way one says, "I love you".


00:04:13.766 --> 00:04:17.094
Where I come from,
at my age...


00:04:18.821 --> 00:04:21.556
It's the way one says,
"I just got knocked up".


00:04:25.343 --> 00:04:29.100
So, you're worried about
what people will think.


00:04:30.441 --> 00:04:32.818
You know, it's two out of three
marriages end in divorce.


00:04:35.257 --> 00:04:38.069
Well, I think you'll find
the...


00:04:38.069 --> 00:04:42.238
Vampire, human divorce rate
is a little lower.


00:04:47.373 --> 00:04:49.084
Just marry me.


00:04:53.349 --> 00:04:54.871
I can't.


00:04:56.865 --> 00:04:58.879
I have to be back at four.


00:05:22.327 --> 00:05:24.820
Four o'clock on the dot.


00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.493
That kid trying to brown nose me
now or something?


00:05:28.529 --> 00:05:32.532
He has a name.
And now he's too punctual for you?


00:05:40.529 --> 00:05:41.717
Okey...


00:05:43.417 --> 00:05:46.409
You understand
why you're being punished, right?


00:05:46.409 --> 00:05:50.311
- I know, I put you through hell.
- Yes, you did.


00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:55.271
But I have other reasons,
for grounding you.


00:05:55.271 --> 00:05:57.307
Like...


00:06:00.818 --> 00:06:04.885
I just want you to get
some separation from him.


00:06:06.606 --> 00:06:08.891
Dad, there is nothing
you can say.


00:06:11.539 --> 00:06:13.571
Edward is in my life.


00:06:15.716 --> 00:06:18.249
Yeah, I'm gathering that.


00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:24.746
So, alright. How about this?
I'll make you a deal.


00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:31.065
You're not grounded anymore,
if...


00:06:31.065 --> 00:06:32.511
You use your
new found freedom...


00:06:32.511 --> 00:06:34.724
to see some
of your other friends too,


00:06:34.724 --> 00:06:38.672
Like...
Like Jacob.


00:06:38.672 --> 00:06:40.344
He's going through
a really tough time right now,


00:06:40.344 --> 00:06:42.524
His Dad's
really worried about him.


00:06:43.051 --> 00:06:44.999
I remember
when that was you.


00:06:47.098 --> 00:06:50.645
You needed a friend,
Jake was there.


00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:58.053
<i>Hey, it's Jake.
Leave a message.</i>


00:07:00.135 --> 00:07:02.035
Jacob hadn't talk to me
in weeks.


00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.860
I wanted to fix it,
he just...


00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.756
He wouldn't give me
the chance.


00:07:18.222 --> 00:07:22.347
<i>"I miss you too.
Doesn't change anything."</i>


00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:01.889
You scared me.


00:08:04.633 --> 00:08:06.935
You're going now
to the reservation.


00:08:06.935 --> 00:08:10.517
How'd you -- ?
Alice...


00:08:13.851 --> 00:08:16.107
Hey,
did you do this to my truck?


00:08:16.507 --> 00:08:20.432
Bella, you have to understand.
Your safety is everything to me.


00:08:20.432 --> 00:08:21.895
Jacob is not gonna hurt me!


00:08:21.895 --> 00:08:24.810
Not intentionally,
but the wolves have no control...


00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:28.055
Edward!
I have...


00:08:28.055 --> 00:08:30.623
Until graduation,
to see him.


00:08:33.383 --> 00:08:37.630
And I'll be one of you,
and he'll hate me forever.


00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.457
I'm sorry.


00:08:54.565 --> 00:08:56.387
- Hey.
- Just in time. Alright, check it out.


00:08:56.387 --> 00:08:58.787
- Alright, let's see what you got.
- My fellow students.


00:08:58.787 --> 00:08:59.619
- Cool.
- Right?


00:08:59.619 --> 00:09:00.989
- Wow.
- Okey, right? -- Cute.


00:09:00.989 --> 00:09:03.864
We are the future.
Anything is possible...


00:09:03.864 --> 00:09:05.548
...If you just believe.
- Nice.


00:09:05.548 --> 00:09:07.206
Blah, blah, blah...


00:09:07.206 --> 00:09:09.086
- Perfect.
- And got your self a speech.


00:09:09.086 --> 00:09:10.205
No, this will be my speech.


00:09:10.205 --> 00:09:12.790
When I want everyone to throw
diplomas at my head.


00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.285
So...
Thank you.


00:09:15.984 --> 00:09:17.533
Ya gotta embrace the cliches,
Jess.


00:09:17.533 --> 00:09:20.043
They have the bread and butter
of all valedictorians.


00:09:20.043 --> 00:09:22.594
And that is why
you are not valedictorian.


00:09:22.594 --> 00:09:26.439
And Jess doesn't need cliches.
Speech is gonna be epic.


00:09:26.439 --> 00:09:28.802
Epic? It'll change lives.


00:09:29.773 --> 00:09:31.538
I decided to throw a party.


00:09:31.538 --> 00:09:35.005
After all, how many times
we gonna graduate high school?


00:09:35.005 --> 00:09:36.853
A party? At your place?


00:09:38.496 --> 00:09:41.457
- I've never seen your house.
- No one's ever seen their house.


00:09:41.457 --> 00:09:43.425
A nother party, Alice?


00:09:43.425 --> 00:09:45.199
- It'll be fun.
- Yeah.


00:09:45.199 --> 00:09:47.017
That's what you said last time.


00:09:51.822 --> 00:09:52.896
- Hey, Angela.
- Yes.


00:09:52.896 --> 00:09:54.601
Do you need some help
with those?


00:10:24.368 --> 00:10:26.707
I know you know what she saw.
Tell me.


00:10:26.707 --> 00:10:28.473
It was nothing.


00:10:29.425 --> 00:10:31.462
You looked worried.


00:10:32.662 --> 00:10:35.984
Just that everyone would notice
how strange Alice is.


00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:40.093
I think that ship sailed
long ago.


00:10:42.276 --> 00:10:43.589
I wonder what's wrong.


00:10:44.102 --> 00:10:46.756
There's someone missing
in Seattle, over a year ago.


00:10:47.054 --> 00:10:49.480
Charlie is doing what he can,
but...


00:10:52.635 --> 00:10:54.362
Do you know something
about this?


00:10:57.511 --> 00:11:00.544
We've been tracking the situation
in Seattle for a while.


00:11:00.939 --> 00:11:04.571
Unexplained disappearances,
killings...


00:11:04.571 --> 00:11:06.668
If the situation gets anymore
conspicuous,


00:11:06.668 --> 00:11:08.616
the Volturi will step in.


00:11:10.788 --> 00:11:13.040
If they go to Seattle,
they can come here.


00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:16.413
- They can see I'm still human.
- We won't get that far.


00:11:16.413 --> 00:11:18.638
But we'll go to Seattle
if we have to.


00:11:20.632 --> 00:11:22.141
I'll fax these down
the first thing.


00:11:22.141 --> 00:11:23.373
Thank you.


00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.552
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:11:28.032 --> 00:11:30.549
- You're ready for dinner?
- Yeah.


00:11:30.549 --> 00:11:33.929
It is still just...
you and I, alright?


00:11:34.521 --> 00:11:36.330
No, I'm just dropping her off.


00:11:37.765 --> 00:11:39.932
- See you later.
- Bye.


00:11:41.432 --> 00:11:43.521
Oh...
Bella.


00:11:43.521 --> 00:11:45.409
My parents wanted to
remind you about the...


00:11:45.409 --> 00:11:47.433
Airline ticket
you got for your birthday.


00:11:47.433 --> 00:11:49.305
What airline ticket?


00:11:50.782 --> 00:11:53.428
A round trip ticket
to see Mom in Florida.


00:11:53.428 --> 00:11:55.733
Wow, that was generous.


00:11:55.733 --> 00:11:58.313
And it expires soon, they say
you might wanna use it this weekend.


00:11:58.313 --> 00:12:01.937
Well, I can't just drop
everything and go.


00:12:01.937 --> 00:12:04.807
It might be your last chance
to see her before you graduate.


00:12:05.299 --> 00:12:07.778
Well. It might not be
a bad idea.


00:12:07.778 --> 00:12:09.034
get out of the town
for a couple of days,


00:12:09.034 --> 00:12:11.313
get some distance.


00:12:12.608 --> 00:12:15.649
Yeah,
I wouldn't mind seeing Mom...


00:12:15.649 --> 00:12:17.859
As long as you
use the companion ticket.


00:12:17.859 --> 00:12:20.342
Wait, just two tickets?


00:12:22.513 --> 00:12:26.458
Super,
That makes me really happy.


00:12:28.946 --> 00:12:31.362
<i>I did wanna see my Mom.</i>


00:12:31.362 --> 00:12:34.807
<i>I wanted to know that her life
was full by satisfying</i>


00:12:37.232 --> 00:12:38.769
Aren't you gonna miss this?


00:12:39.846 --> 00:12:44.010
Don't you just feel the vitamin D
soaking up in your pores?


00:12:46.957 --> 00:12:49.145
Yeah, I'm gonna miss this.


00:12:51.132 --> 00:12:54.165
You know, colleges in Florida
are a lot sunnier.


00:12:58.479 --> 00:13:01.169
I'm just saying,
if you go to university of Alaska...


00:13:01.169 --> 00:13:02.785
I'm never gonna see you.


00:13:07.869 --> 00:13:10.037
They have a really great
science program.


00:13:10.905 --> 00:13:13.154
You mean Edward program.


00:13:15.555 --> 00:13:17.864
The way he watches you...


00:13:17.864 --> 00:13:19.395
It's like he's willing to leap
in front of you,


00:13:19.395 --> 00:13:21.464
and take a bullet
or something.


00:13:22.309 --> 00:13:23.896
Is that a bad thing?


00:13:24.784 --> 00:13:27.296
It's an intense thing.


00:13:27.296 --> 00:13:29.012
You're different with him.


00:13:30.381 --> 00:13:33.985
If he moves, you move.
Like magnets.


00:13:35.496 --> 00:13:37.847
I don't know, we're  just...


00:13:37.847 --> 00:13:40.407
In love.
I get it.


00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:42.168
I just want to make sure,


00:13:42.168 --> 00:13:44.706
you're making
the right choices for you.


00:13:46.079 --> 00:13:48.435
You know, cause you're the one
who's gonna have to live with him.


00:13:52.251 --> 00:13:55.249
Alright, enough with the heavy.


00:14:02.093 --> 00:14:05.119
- Mom.
- Congraduation.


00:14:05.119 --> 00:14:06.664
I didn't want you
to spending you're money.


00:14:06.664 --> 00:14:08.417
I didn't, come on.


00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:25.768
Are these all our old trip T-shirts?
- Emm. -- Get out!


00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:28.513
I saved'em all.
I thought they'd make a good quilt.


00:14:28.513 --> 00:14:30.847
To keep you warm up in Alaska.


00:14:31.601 --> 00:14:34.680
Remember this one?
Ensanada.


00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.380
- The snake pit.
- Yep.


00:14:37.328 --> 00:14:39.319
But this one is my favourite.
Here...


00:14:40.158 --> 00:14:42.657
The three-headed lobster
in Maine.


00:14:42.657 --> 00:14:45.323
- This is amazing.
- No, honey. I'm glad you've like it.


00:14:45.323 --> 00:14:47.430
I just figured, you know,
when you get older, have kids,


00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:48.882
We can add to it.
Maybe go visit...


00:14:48.882 --> 00:14:51.197
the world's largest catsup bottle
or something.


00:14:51.197 --> 00:14:53.203
- Thanks
- Oh...


00:14:55.099 --> 00:14:56.863
I'm glad you like it.


00:14:57.408 --> 00:15:01.356
I just thought, you should have
a little piece of me, up there in Alaska.


00:15:03.426 --> 00:15:05.747
- Mom.
- Yeah.


00:15:09.121 --> 00:15:14.388
- I miss you.
- Oh, honey. I miss you too.


00:15:31.679 --> 00:15:33.778
You sure this is
where you saw her?


00:15:34.817 --> 00:15:36.796
She's almost here.


00:15:49.582 --> 00:15:50.845
On your left!


00:16:26.553 --> 00:16:29.695
Wait!
She's in their territory.


00:16:31.212 --> 00:16:32.885
She'll get away!


00:16:34.136 --> 00:16:35.660
No she won't!


00:17:11.285 --> 00:17:12.949
Emmett, no!


00:17:45.802 --> 00:17:47.409
Did you regret going?


00:17:49.269 --> 00:17:50.550
No.


00:17:51.868 --> 00:17:56.484
It was really great to see my mom.
Just really hard saying goodbye.


00:17:57.400 --> 00:18:01.233
- It doesn't have to be goodbye.
- Is that why you ask me to go?


00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.877
You thought
I was gonna change my mind.


00:18:05.322 --> 00:18:07.614
I'm always hoping for that.


00:18:09.209 --> 00:18:10.511
What?


00:18:11.799 --> 00:18:14.733
If I asked you to stay in the car,
would you?


00:18:21.108 --> 00:18:22.589
Of course not.


00:18:34.852 --> 00:18:35.892
Hey.


00:18:37.352 --> 00:18:41.364
- Charlie said you left town.
- Yeah. To visit my Mom, why?


00:18:42.165 --> 00:18:44.175
Just checking to see
if you're still human.


00:18:45.966 --> 00:18:47.470
I'm coming here to warn you.


00:18:48.205 --> 00:18:50.734
If your kind
come on our land again...


00:18:50.734 --> 00:18:51.972
Wait, what?


00:18:54.595 --> 00:18:57.968
- You didn't tell her?
- Just leave it alone, Jacob.


00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:00.376
Tell me what?


00:19:01.376 --> 00:19:04.690
Emmett and Paul
had a misunderstanding,


00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.427
there is nothing
to worry about.


00:19:06.427 --> 00:19:08.233
Listen to you.


00:19:08.233 --> 00:19:10.301
Did you lie
to get her out of town, too?


00:19:10.301 --> 00:19:14.245
You should leave.
Now.


00:19:14.245 --> 00:19:16.329
She has a right to know.


00:19:17.022 --> 00:19:19.572
She is the one
the red-head wants.


00:19:20.856 --> 00:19:22.574
Victoria?


00:19:23.558 --> 00:19:28.591
- Alices's vision.
- I was trying to protect you.


00:19:28.591 --> 00:19:30.770
By lying to me.


00:19:33.287 --> 00:19:35.551
Okey. We're gonna talk
about this, but...


00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:37.329
You!


00:19:37.892 --> 00:19:39.700
Why haven't you
called me back?


00:19:42.812 --> 00:19:45.234
I had nothing to say.


00:19:47.036 --> 00:19:49.658
- Well, I have tons. Hold on.
- Hey.


00:19:51.546 --> 00:19:52.748
Bella.


00:19:53.203 --> 00:19:56.122
- Edward, you have to trust me.
- I do trust you.


00:19:57.298 --> 00:19:59.055
It's him I don't trust.


00:20:10.255 --> 00:20:13.311
Lose the grin, Jacob.
We're just going for a ride.


00:20:13.311 --> 00:20:15.286
Hold on tight.


00:20:28.755 --> 00:20:30.716
Are you sure,
this is a good idea?


00:20:33.034 --> 00:20:35.237
I'm a "vampire girl",
remember?


00:20:36.196 --> 00:20:38.805
- Look who's back.
- Whatup, Bella?


00:20:38.805 --> 00:20:42.524
- Quil, you too?
- Yep. Finally made the pack.


00:20:42.524 --> 00:20:43.601
I'm glad you're here, Bella.


00:20:43.601 --> 00:20:46.275
Maybe we can get a break from
Jake's obsessive inner monologue.


00:20:46.275 --> 00:20:47.861
"I wish Bella would call".


00:20:47.861 --> 00:20:50.495
- "I wish Bella wouldn't call".
- "Maybe I should call Bella".


00:20:50.495 --> 00:20:52.618
"Maybe I should call Bella
and hang up".


00:20:53.632 --> 00:20:55.567
Alright, you can shut up now.


00:20:58.470 --> 00:21:02.038
Bella, this is Leah Clearwater.
Harry's daughter.


00:21:02.643 --> 00:21:05.897
Hey.
I'm really sorry about your father.


00:21:05.897 --> 00:21:08.903
If you're here to torture Jacob
some more, feel free to leave.


00:21:12.245 --> 00:21:13.959
Fun, isn't she?


00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:17.512
- Bella... Hi.
- Hey.


00:21:17.512 --> 00:21:20.268
I was wondering when we'd see
your face around here again.


00:21:20.268 --> 00:21:22.209
Yeah, same here.


00:21:22.209 --> 00:21:23.542
Sam, we're good?


00:21:23.542 --> 00:21:26.759
We're good. She won't be getting
through our line anytime soon.


00:21:38.085 --> 00:21:40.862
So, when did Leah
joined the pack?


00:21:40.862 --> 00:21:45.445
Around when her Dad died.
Her brother Seth, also phased.


00:21:45.445 --> 00:21:49.574
He's only fifteen.
One of the youngest we've had.


00:21:49.574 --> 00:21:52.582
Sam keeps him home studying,
but he's chomping at the bit.


00:21:53.908 --> 00:21:55.777
Wish it was Leah
who'd stay home.


00:21:56.699 --> 00:21:58.225
Come on,
don't be such a guy.


00:21:58.921 --> 00:22:04.821
No, it's... It's not a chick thing.
It's... You know, a triangle thing.


00:22:05.101 --> 00:22:08.928
We all have to live
the Leah, Sam, Emily pain-fest.


00:22:10.244 --> 00:22:12.356
Wolf telepathy, remember?


00:22:12.356 --> 00:22:15.117
So, Sam dumps Leah
for Emily?


00:22:15.117 --> 00:22:20.274
It wasn't like that.
Sam hates himself for hurting Leah.


00:22:20.274 --> 00:22:22.714
But, Emily was The One.


00:22:23.553 --> 00:22:26.227
Yeah, I guess it's sort of
chooses you sometimes.


00:22:28.445 --> 00:22:32.845
It's more than some crush, Bella.
Sam imprinted on Emily.


00:22:34.486 --> 00:22:36.160
Do I want to know what that is?


00:22:45.934 --> 00:22:49.661
Imprinting on someone
is like...


00:22:50.934 --> 00:22:56.150
Like when you see her,
everything changes.


00:22:57.613 --> 00:23:01.683
All of a sudden, it's not
gravity holding you to the planet.


00:23:02.476 --> 00:23:03.933
It's her.


00:23:04.656 --> 00:23:10.056
Nothing else matters.
You would do anything...


00:23:11.332 --> 00:23:14.204
Be anything for her.


00:23:16.097 --> 00:23:18.668
It sounds like
you know the feeling.


00:23:22.244 --> 00:23:27.344
Have you...
imprinted on someone?


00:23:32.778 --> 00:23:34.877
You'd know if I had.


00:23:38.465 --> 00:23:41.234
I just have a direct line
to Sam's thoughts.


00:23:43.245 --> 00:23:47.219
So for now, you're...
still you.


00:23:49.458 --> 00:23:53.864
- And you're still you.
- Yeah.


00:23:59.327 --> 00:24:01.407
Until graduation.


00:24:02.442 --> 00:24:04.097
graduation?


00:24:05.407 --> 00:24:07.122
You knew
this was gonna happen.


00:24:07.122 --> 00:24:08.872
Not in a month!


00:24:10.784 --> 00:24:15.057
I mean, not before you've...
you've even lived!


00:24:16.097 --> 00:24:18.331
Or before I could...


00:24:21.712 --> 00:24:26.466
For a second, just a second,
I thought...


00:24:27.280 --> 00:24:30.675
But he's got his hooks in you
so deep.


00:24:31.261 --> 00:24:35.241
- I decided this, not him.
- Bella, they're not even a live!


00:24:36.616 --> 00:24:38.592
It makes me sick!


00:24:40.729 --> 00:24:43.818
Better you really be dead
than one of them.


00:24:56.775 --> 00:24:58.707
I can't believe you said that.


00:25:03.024 --> 00:25:05.266
Edward was right,
I shouldn't have come.


00:25:05.266 --> 00:25:08.459
Bella, come on.
Please.


00:25:11.521 --> 00:25:13.458
I'm sorry.


00:26:22.170 --> 00:26:23.893
You know...


00:26:23.893 --> 00:26:26.404
Edward could at least
respect meal times.


00:26:27.340 --> 00:26:29.691
I was just with Jake.


00:26:29.691 --> 00:26:30.891
Oh...
Good.


00:26:37.641 --> 00:26:41.272
I'll just give you two
some privacy then.


00:26:43.355 --> 00:26:44.037
Hey.


00:26:44.037 --> 00:26:45.808
Do you understand
how worried I've been?


00:26:45.808 --> 00:26:47.131
I was perfectly safe.


00:26:47.131 --> 00:26:49.617
I almost break the treaty
to make sure of it.


00:26:50.592 --> 00:26:53.021
- I know, I smell like a dog. I'm sorry.
- No, no. Something's wrong.


00:27:00.722 --> 00:27:03.788
- Edward, what's wrong?
- Someone's been in here.


00:27:09.683 --> 00:27:13.027
Who was it?
Someone we know?


00:27:13.027 --> 00:27:16.152
Just a stranger.
I didn't recognize his scent.


00:27:16.152 --> 00:27:17.759
A nomad passing through?


00:27:17.759 --> 00:27:20.451
A passer-by wouldn't have left
Bella's father alive.


00:27:20.451 --> 00:27:23.384
His scent disappeared about five miles
south of Bella's house.


00:27:25.192 --> 00:27:28.492
- Someone's orchestrating this.
- Victoria?


00:27:29.292 --> 00:27:32.930
- I would've seen her deciding.
- It has to be the Volturi.


00:27:32.930 --> 00:27:35.644
I don't think
it's the Volturi either.


00:27:35.644 --> 00:27:37.309
I've been watching
Aro's decisions, too.


00:27:37.309 --> 00:27:38.639
So we keep looking.


00:27:38.639 --> 00:27:41.305
We also take shifts,
guarding Bella at her house.


00:27:41.693 --> 00:27:44.690
- A nother protection detail?
- Rosalie.


00:27:45.909 --> 00:27:47.445
No, she's right.


00:27:47.445 --> 00:27:50.261
You can't protect me,
watch my dad...


00:27:50.261 --> 00:27:51.944
and search for the intruder.


00:27:51.944 --> 00:27:55.535
- And for Victoria.
- And keep yourselves fed.


00:27:55.535 --> 00:27:57.277
I'm not leaving you here
defenseless.


00:27:57.277 --> 00:27:59.325
Well, I'm not gonna
let you starve.


00:28:00.411 --> 00:28:04.369
And I wouldn't be unprotected,
I have...


00:28:04.369 --> 00:28:06.257
What?


00:28:13.494 --> 00:28:16.454
Whoever it was,
he left his stink behind.


00:28:16.454 --> 00:28:19.232
It'll be hard to miss
when we cross it again.


00:28:19.232 --> 00:28:22.310
- We'll handle it from here.
- We don't need you to handle anything.


00:28:23.112 --> 00:28:26.140
- Or anyone.
- I could care less what you need.


00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:28.023
Alright, we're done here.


00:28:28.023 --> 00:28:30.907
- No, you're done here.
- Stop!


00:28:30.907 --> 00:28:34.228
I'm tired of this.
From now on I'm Switzerland, Okay?


00:28:35.729 --> 00:28:40.350
<i>Edward hated the idea,
but it wasn't about rivalry anymore.</i>


00:28:40.996 --> 00:28:43.673
<i>It was about my safety,
and Charlie's.</i>


00:28:44.844 --> 00:28:48.327
<i>In the days that followed
I got them to at least try to work together.</i>


00:28:54.258 --> 00:28:56.718
<i>The wolves took over
so the Cullen's can hunt.</i>


00:28:59.951 --> 00:29:02.470
<i>It wasn't exactly
an easy alliance.</i>


00:29:19.006 --> 00:29:20.644
Doesn't he own a shirt?


00:29:25.543 --> 00:29:27.554
I'm good here,
you should go.


00:29:27.554 --> 00:29:32.860
- I'm not gonna be going long.
- Don't rush. You need to hunt.


00:29:49.109 --> 00:29:51.245
Maybe you rush a little bit.


00:29:56.559 --> 00:29:58.570
- Hey, beautiful.
- Hi.


00:30:09.339 --> 00:30:13.684
So, whaddaya wanna do today?
Bike, hike, hang?


00:30:13.684 --> 00:30:16.460
Your call.
Or we're going to a party tonight.


00:30:19.483 --> 00:30:23.739
You sure this is okay?
I really hate being a party crasher.


00:30:24.620 --> 00:30:27.243
Technically,
you're a Council Meeting crasher.


00:30:27.966 --> 00:30:33.066
See. The Council leaders,
Dad, Quil's grandpa, and Sue Clearwater.


00:30:33.698 --> 00:30:35.589
She took over for Harry
when he died.


00:30:35.589 --> 00:30:37.386
Okay, I should not be here.


00:30:38.205 --> 00:30:41.867
You're okay.
I thought...


00:30:41.867 --> 00:30:44.862
I mean, they thought it would be
good for you to hear the histories.


00:30:45.600 --> 00:30:50.600
The histories? The tribe's histories?
Aren't they secret?


00:30:51.663 --> 00:30:55.220
We all got a role to play.
And you're a part of this.


00:30:55.950 --> 00:30:59.016
I mean, it's the first time Seth,
Leah and Quil are hearing them, too.


00:30:59.016 --> 00:31:02.414
But you are the first outsider.
Ever.


00:31:04.551 --> 00:31:06.345
If I haven't known that,
I wouldn't believe you.


00:31:08.433 --> 00:31:10.974
- And would've dressed better.
- Jake.


00:31:12.038 --> 00:31:14.997
- Hey.
- It's about time, you got here.


00:31:14.997 --> 00:31:18.148
Paul's been hoovering the grub.
But, I saved you some burgers.


00:31:18.148 --> 00:31:20.373
Good looking out, Bro.


00:31:20.373 --> 00:31:23.371
Bella, this is Seth Clearwater,
Leah's brother.


00:31:23.371 --> 00:31:27.473
- Newest member of the pack.
- Newest, bestest, brightest.


00:31:27.473 --> 00:31:29.114
And slowest.


00:31:31.783 --> 00:31:33.992
- Come on. Your dad's about to start.
- Alright.


00:31:36.293 --> 00:31:39.368
The Quileutes have been a small tribe
from the beginning...


00:31:40.492 --> 00:31:43.098
But we've always had magic in
our blood.


00:31:45.246 --> 00:31:47.624
We were great spirit warriors...


00:31:47.624 --> 00:31:52.724
Shape shifters,
that transform into the powerful wolf.


00:31:54.190 --> 00:31:57.789
This enabled us to scare off
our enemies,


00:31:57.789 --> 00:32:00.395
and protect our tribe.


00:32:01.978 --> 00:32:06.978
One day our warriors
came across a creature...


00:32:08.068 --> 00:32:13.168
<i>It looked like a man,
but it was hard like stone,</i>


00:32:13.168 --> 00:32:15.524
<i>and cold as ice...</i>


00:32:35.154 --> 00:32:39.322
Our warriors' sharp teeth,
finally tore it apart...


00:32:39.322 --> 00:32:43.160
But only fire
would completely destroy it.


00:32:43.942 --> 00:32:47.733
They lived in fear,
the Cold Man was not alone.


00:32:48.955 --> 00:32:50.579
And they were right.


00:32:54.522 --> 00:32:57.782
<i>She took her vengeance out
on the village.</i>


00:33:00.265 --> 00:33:02.616
<i>Our elder chief,
Taha Aki,</i>


00:33:02.616 --> 00:33:06.111
<i>was the only spirit warrior left
to save the tribe,</i>


00:33:06.111 --> 00:33:08.893
<i>after his son was killed.</i>


00:33:20.125 --> 00:33:23.879
<i>Taha Aki's Third Wife could sees
that he would lose...</i>


00:33:24.915 --> 00:33:28.841
<i>The Third Wife
was no magical being,</i>


00:33:28.841 --> 00:33:31.640
<i>no special powers, but one...</i>


00:33:33.176 --> 00:33:35.057
Courage.


00:33:45.949 --> 00:33:49.256
The Third Wife's sacrifice
distracted the Cold Woman,


00:33:49.256 --> 00:33:52.890
long enough for Taha Aki
to destroy her.


00:33:53.396 --> 00:33:55.531
She saved the tribe.


00:33:56.122 --> 00:33:59.412
Over time,
our enemies have disappeared.


00:34:00.299 --> 00:34:02.268
But one remains...


00:34:03.672 --> 00:34:05.817
The Cold Ones.


00:34:08.031 --> 00:34:10.573
Our magic awakens
when they near.


00:34:10.573 --> 00:34:14.757
And we sense it now,
we feel the threat in our blood.


00:34:16.426 --> 00:34:18.600
Something terrible is coming.


00:34:20.603 --> 00:34:25.703
And we must all be ready.
All of us.


00:34:52.703 --> 00:34:54.578
What did you do to me?


00:34:58.891 --> 00:35:03.015
- I'm so...
- Yeah, I know...


00:35:04.339 --> 00:35:06.063
We'll find you someone
to drink.


00:35:14.276 --> 00:35:17.555
Just try not to get killed,
will you?


00:35:20.392 --> 00:35:22.514
I'm gonna need numbers.


00:35:23.911 --> 00:35:26.030
<i>Seattle is in a state of terror...</i>


00:35:26.030 --> 00:35:29.961
<i>Police are baffled by the
escalating murders and disappearances.</i>


00:35:29.961 --> 00:35:34.307
<i>Theories range from a vicious new gang
to a wildly active serial killer...</i>


00:35:34.307 --> 00:35:36.832
<i>- Reporting live, Dawn Chubai. CNN.
- It's getting worse.</i>


00:35:36.832 --> 00:35:38.949
We're going to have
to do something.


00:35:38.949 --> 00:35:43.168
It takes more than one of our kind
to cause the damage they're reporting.


00:35:43.168 --> 00:35:47.220
Quite a few more.
They're undisciplined, conspicuous...


00:35:47.220 --> 00:35:48.979
It's a Newborns.


00:35:50.255 --> 00:35:52.120
What, like new vampires?


00:35:52.120 --> 00:35:54.305
In their first few months
after the change.


00:35:54.305 --> 00:35:56.817
That's when we're at our most
uncontrollable,


00:35:56.817 --> 00:36:00.868
vicious, insane with thirst.


00:36:00.868 --> 00:36:03.584
Something to look forward to.


00:36:05.078 --> 00:36:08.615
No one has trained these newborns,
but this isn't random.


00:36:09.029 --> 00:36:10.890
Someone's creating an army.


00:36:11.601 --> 00:36:13.723
Oh, now we definitely
going to Seattle.


00:36:14.657 --> 00:36:16.687
An Army of vampires?


00:36:16.687 --> 00:36:18.361
And they've been created
to fight someone.


00:36:18.361 --> 00:36:20.271
We're the only clan
even close to Seattle.


00:36:20.271 --> 00:36:21.475
Regardless,
of who are they were may,


00:36:21.475 --> 00:36:23.834
if we don't put a stop to them,
the Volturi will.


00:36:24.986 --> 00:36:27.311
I'm surprised
they've let it go on this long.


00:36:27.311 --> 00:36:28.843
Maybe they're behind it.


00:36:29.843 --> 00:36:32.589
In Italy,
I read Aro's mind...


00:36:32.589 --> 00:36:34.306
He wants me and Alice
to join him...


00:36:34.306 --> 00:36:37.613
He knows we'd never choose him
as long as our family is still alive.


00:36:37.613 --> 00:36:40.300
An army
could solve that for him.


00:36:48.840 --> 00:36:52.368
Hey.
Did you eat dinner yet?


00:36:54.275 --> 00:36:56.699
Um... no...
I haven't.


00:36:59.750 --> 00:37:04.605
This kid Riley Biers,
disappeared over a year ago.


00:37:05.131 --> 00:37:09.091
And his poor parents been papering
Seattle with these things ever since.


00:37:10.601 --> 00:37:12.516
You think
they should just give up?


00:37:15.298 --> 00:37:18.270
I wouldn't.
If it were you...


00:37:20.363 --> 00:37:22.053
Not ever.


00:37:27.838 --> 00:37:29.963
<i>I have to figure out
what to tell people...</i>


00:37:30.895 --> 00:37:33.286
Whu I won't be home
for Christmases.


00:37:34.601 --> 00:37:37.063
Why I won't visit.


00:37:38.662 --> 00:37:40.978
Why they'll never see me again.


00:37:41.424 --> 00:37:46.025
After a few decades,
everyone you know will be dead.


00:37:48.094 --> 00:37:50.107
Problem solved.


00:37:54.606 --> 00:37:57.159
Why are you so against me
becoming like you?


00:37:57.862 --> 00:37:59.857
I've told you.


00:38:02.263 --> 00:38:06.763
Be honest with me.
There's more.


00:38:07.385 --> 00:38:12.285
I know the consequences,
of this choice you're making.


00:38:16.993 --> 00:38:22.844
I've lived through it,
and to let you suffer that.


00:38:24.450 --> 00:38:27.323
You believe I have a soul...


00:38:27.323 --> 00:38:29.338
I don't.


00:38:31.506 --> 00:38:36.206
But to risk yours, just for the sake
of never having to lose you.


00:38:38.605 --> 00:38:41.281
It's the most selfish thing
I'll ever do.


00:38:45.373 --> 00:38:49.425
I thought, maybe you were afraid
that I'll be too different.


00:38:51.445 --> 00:38:55.365
Unlike. I won't be, you know...
warm.


00:38:55.365 --> 00:38:57.413
And won't smell the same.


00:39:06.347 --> 00:39:09.250
You'll always be my Bella.


00:39:29.769 --> 00:39:32.968
My Bella, just less fragile.


00:39:43.289 --> 00:39:45.430
Gosh, it's so pretty here.


00:39:50.966 --> 00:39:54.141
So, Alice is planning
a big graduation party.


00:39:55.146 --> 00:39:56.913
Which you're invited to.


00:40:00.858 --> 00:40:03.845
Yeah,
I figured that.


00:40:11.293 --> 00:40:12.548
What?


00:40:14.366 --> 00:40:16.582
I just wanted to do this
differently.


00:40:17.402 --> 00:40:18.833
Smoother.


00:40:20.312 --> 00:40:22.287
But now, I'm out of time.


00:40:23.631 --> 00:40:25.009
To what?


00:40:25.723 --> 00:40:28.115
You need to hear the truth,
Bella.


00:40:28.915 --> 00:40:31.448
Understand all your options.


00:40:32.902 --> 00:40:34.727
You need to know...


00:40:36.114 --> 00:40:38.869
That I'm in love with you.


00:40:39.919 --> 00:40:43.177
And I want you to choose me,
instead of him.


00:40:44.942 --> 00:40:46.743
I thought you understood.


00:40:49.898 --> 00:40:52.445
- I don't feel that way for you.
- I don't buy it.


00:40:52.445 --> 00:40:54.061
What don't you buy?


00:40:55.960 --> 00:40:58.035
That's how I feel.


00:40:58.035 --> 00:41:01.882
You feel something else for me,
you just won't admit it.


00:41:02.887 --> 00:41:07.987
So I'm not giving up.
I'm gonna fight for you.


00:41:10.666 --> 00:41:13.106
Until your heart stops beating.


00:41:13.737 --> 00:41:15.430
Well, then you're not gonna have
to fight for long.


00:41:15.430 --> 00:41:17.827
You're rushing into it because
you're afraid you'll change your mind.


00:41:17.827 --> 00:41:19.330
No, I'm not.


00:41:20.853 --> 00:41:22.248
I know what I want.


00:41:24.076 --> 00:41:27.001
You wouldn't have
to change for me, Bella.


00:41:27.801 --> 00:41:30.360
Or say goodbye to anybody.


00:41:31.093 --> 00:41:34.099
I can give you more than him.


00:41:34.586 --> 00:41:37.905
I mean, he probably can't even
kiss you without hurting you.


00:41:40.328 --> 00:41:42.718
Feel that?


00:41:42.718 --> 00:41:47.031
Flesh and blood and warmth.


00:42:11.154 --> 00:42:11.910
Edward!


00:42:11.910 --> 00:42:14.380
If you ever touch her
against her will again!


00:42:14.380 --> 00:42:16.347
- Don't do this!
- She's not sure what she wants!


00:42:16.347 --> 00:42:17.826
- Don't do this!
- Well, let me give you a clue!


00:42:17.826 --> 00:42:21.917
- Wait for her to say the words!
- Fine! And she will!


00:42:21.917 --> 00:42:24.922
- Jacob. Just go, okay!
- Hey, hey, hey, hey...


00:42:24.922 --> 00:42:29.439
Easy guys, easy.
Let's take it down a notch. Alright?


00:42:32.487 --> 00:42:34.108
What's going on?


00:42:37.519 --> 00:42:39.316
I kissed Bella.


00:42:43.215 --> 00:42:45.497
And she broke her hand...


00:42:46.821 --> 00:42:49.024
Punching my face.


00:42:50.814 --> 00:42:53.206
Total misunderstanding.


00:42:55.040 --> 00:42:58.502
It's just a sprain,
should heal fairly quickly.


00:43:00.129 --> 00:43:03.093
Trying to walk and chew gum
at the same time again, Bella?


00:43:04.544 --> 00:43:07.641
- I punched a werewolf in the face.
- Bad ass...


00:43:07.641 --> 00:43:10.817
You're gonna be
one tough little newborn.


00:43:10.817 --> 00:43:13.281
Tough enough to take you on.


00:43:18.832 --> 00:43:20.978
Don't worry about it.


00:43:23.437 --> 00:43:25.561
Okay, any Leads?


00:43:25.561 --> 00:43:29.947
No sign of the intruder. But Victoria
continues to make appearances.


00:43:37.455 --> 00:43:40.690
Go blather to someone else
about the joys of becoming a newborn.


00:43:44.452 --> 00:43:48.249
Okay.
Rosalie...


00:43:50.467 --> 00:43:53.691
I don't understand what I did,
to make you hate me so much.


00:43:56.584 --> 00:43:58.455
I don't hate you.


00:44:00.852 --> 00:44:03.613
I don't particularly like you,
but...


00:44:08.360 --> 00:44:12.745
- Bella, I envy you.
- What?


00:44:13.977 --> 00:44:16.454
- That's ridiculous.
- No, it's not.


00:44:18.513 --> 00:44:21.772
You have a choice.
I didn't.


00:44:22.635 --> 00:44:25.949
None of us did. But you do,
and you're choosing wrong.


00:44:27.344 --> 00:44:30.457
I don't care how miserable
your human life is.


00:44:31.186 --> 00:44:34.368
My life is not miserable.


00:44:37.027 --> 00:44:40.652
It's not perfect,
but nobody's life is perfect.


00:44:40.652 --> 00:44:44.952
Mine was.
Absolutely perfect.


00:44:46.491 --> 00:44:48.740
Everything as I still wanted.


00:44:49.611 --> 00:44:51.696
To be married,
with a nice house and a husband...


00:44:51.696 --> 00:44:53.778
to kiss me when he came home.


00:44:53.778 --> 00:44:55.931
A family of my own.


00:44:56.615 --> 00:44:59.615
<i>Royce King was
the most eligible bachelor in town.</i>


00:45:01.209 --> 00:45:02.977
<i>I barely knew him.</i>


00:45:07.287 --> 00:45:11.800
<i>But I was young.
I was in love with the idea of love.</i>


00:45:12.807 --> 00:45:16.371
<i>On the last night of my life,
I left a friend's house late.</i>


00:45:16.371 --> 00:45:19.703
<i>- I wasn't far from home.
- Here she is.</i>


00:45:19.703 --> 00:45:22.704
Hey, Rose!
Come over here!


00:45:22.704 --> 00:45:24.393
Here, hold this.


00:45:24.980 --> 00:45:28.733
Hey, come over here.
We've been waiting for you.


00:45:30.354 --> 00:45:32.387
Here she is


00:45:34.258 --> 00:45:35.474
Royce.


00:45:36.609 --> 00:45:38.426
You're drunk.


00:45:38.426 --> 00:45:41.892
Isn't she lovely, John?
I told you she was a looker.


00:45:41.892 --> 00:45:44.812
It's hard to say
with all those clothes on.


00:45:44.812 --> 00:45:49.115
What do you say, Rose?
Why don't we take off a few layers?


00:45:49.115 --> 00:45:51.343
Stop it!...


00:45:53.586 --> 00:45:56.134
I'll see you tomorrow.
Sober.


00:45:57.807 --> 00:45:59.346
Hey, where do you think
you're going?


00:45:59.346 --> 00:46:03.458
- Stop it! Just stop it! Let go! Stop it!
- Comeback! Hey, you'll do as I say!


00:46:08.814 --> 00:46:12.209
They left me in the street,
thinking I was dead.


00:46:12.209 --> 00:46:14.258
Believe me, I wanted to be.


00:46:15.807 --> 00:46:18.310
Carlisle found me,
he smelled all the blood...


00:46:18.310 --> 00:46:21.212
- Thought he was helping me.
- I'm sorry.


00:46:23.985 --> 00:46:26.197
I got my revenge on them.


00:46:27.815 --> 00:46:29.812
One at a time.


00:46:29.812 --> 00:46:33.203
I saved Royce for last,
so he'd know I was coming.


00:46:51.237 --> 00:46:53.843
I was a little theatrical back then.


00:47:02.452 --> 00:47:04.700
Things got better
after I found Emmett.


00:47:07.772 --> 00:47:09.710
But we'll always be this.


00:47:13.726 --> 00:47:18.047
Frozen,
never moving forward.


00:47:19.459 --> 00:47:23.492
That's what I miss the most,
the possibilities.


00:47:24.270 --> 00:47:26.488
Sitting on a front porch
somewhere,


00:47:27.063 --> 00:47:29.726
Emmett gray haired
by my side,


00:47:29.726 --> 00:47:32.512
surrounded by
our grandchildren,


00:47:33.698 --> 00:47:35.819
their laughter.


00:47:37.446 --> 00:47:40.414
I understand,
that's what you want.


00:47:47.224 --> 00:47:50.960
But there's nothing
I'll ever gonna want, more...


00:47:52.873 --> 00:47:54.785
than Edward.


00:47:55.165 --> 00:47:56.844
You're wrong again.


00:47:59.009 --> 00:48:02.230
After you've been changed,
there's one thing you'll want more...


00:48:03.342 --> 00:48:05.365
One thing you'll kill for...


00:48:07.597 --> 00:48:09.342
Blood.


00:48:14.820 --> 00:48:18.234
What did I say,
about low profile?


00:48:30.577 --> 00:48:32.506
Something's coming...


00:48:34.540 --> 00:48:39.214
Something...
Bigger than any of us alone.


00:48:40.032 --> 00:48:42.007
And if you can't...


00:48:43.146 --> 00:48:45.462
control yourselves...


00:48:47.325 --> 00:48:49.260
We're all going to die.


00:48:53.780 --> 00:48:56.469
What's done is done,
just...


00:48:58.814 --> 00:49:01.115
clean up after yourselves.


00:49:09.759 --> 00:49:12.890
They've already drawn
too much attention.


00:49:12.890 --> 00:49:15.201
So has our "inaction".


00:49:15.201 --> 00:49:18.736
Others may begin to question
the Volturi's effectiveness.


00:49:19.730 --> 00:49:21.427
Let them.


00:49:26.736 --> 00:49:29.055
Maybe we should consult
with Aro.


00:49:33.953 --> 00:49:36.326
Aro's decisions
are being watched.


00:49:38.401 --> 00:49:40.280
We must decide.


00:49:42.374 --> 00:49:46.320
Then decide sister.
It's time.


00:49:47.581 --> 00:49:49.448
Yes, it is.


00:49:54.263 --> 00:49:58.102
Either we let them do
what they were created for...


00:49:58.102 --> 00:49:59.859
Or we end them.


00:50:00.888 --> 00:50:03.474
Decisions, decisions...


00:50:13.266 --> 00:50:14.379
When we were five,


00:50:14.379 --> 00:50:17.712
they asked us what we wanted to be
when we grew up...


00:50:17.712 --> 00:50:22.371
Our answers were things like
astronaut, president...


00:50:22.371 --> 00:50:25.172
Or in my case, a princess.


00:50:25.172 --> 00:50:27.711
When we were ten,
they asked again,


00:50:27.711 --> 00:50:30.765
and we answered,
rock star, cowboy,


00:50:30.765 --> 00:50:33.603
or in my case,
a gold medalist.


00:50:33.603 --> 00:50:37.015
But now that we've grown up,
they want a serious answer.


00:50:38.072 --> 00:50:40.862
Well, how about this...


00:50:40.862 --> 00:50:42.935
who the hell knows?


00:50:46.698 --> 00:50:48.899
This isn't the time to make
hard and fast decisions,


00:50:48.899 --> 00:50:51.573
this is the time
to make mistakes.


00:50:51.573 --> 00:50:54.675
Take the wrong train
and get stuck somewhere.


00:50:54.675 --> 00:50:58.144
Fall in love,
a lot.


00:50:58.772 --> 00:51:02.985
Major in philosophy, because there's
no way to make a career out of that.


00:51:02.985 --> 00:51:06.500
Change your mind, and change it again,
because nothing is permanent.


00:51:07.675 --> 00:51:10.167
So, make as many mistakes
as you can.


00:51:10.958 --> 00:51:13.414
That way, someday,
when they ask what we wanna be...


00:51:14.128 --> 00:51:19.105
we won't have to guess.
We'll know.


00:51:46.447 --> 00:51:48.274
You've made it!


00:51:48.274 --> 00:51:50.749
- Hey.
- What'd you think of my speech?


00:51:50.749 --> 00:51:53.327
Too easy-breezy, too self-helpful?
You may admit it.


00:51:53.757 --> 00:51:56.614
- No, you pretty much nailed it.
- Yeah?


00:51:56.614 --> 00:52:00.970
- It's like I was born to lead, right?
- Oh, great. I love this song, let's go.


00:52:25.648 --> 00:52:29.437
- What are you doing here?
- You invited me, remember?


00:52:30.166 --> 00:52:32.744
Was my right hook
too subtle for you?


00:52:32.744 --> 00:52:34.966
That was me
uninviting you.


00:52:34.966 --> 00:52:38.986
Look, Bella. I'm sorry...
about, you know...


00:52:40.030 --> 00:52:43.370
The kiss and your hand...


00:52:43.370 --> 00:52:44.872
I'd blame it on the whole
inner animal thing...


00:52:44.872 --> 00:52:49.618
But it was really just... me.
Being an ass.


00:52:50.457 --> 00:52:52.212
I'm really sorry.


00:52:53.567 --> 00:52:55.134
I brought you something.


00:52:55.653 --> 00:52:59.315
A graduation present.
I made it myself.


00:52:59.870 --> 00:53:03.108
Oh...
You made this?


00:53:04.053 --> 00:53:07.230
It's really pretty.
Thanks.


00:53:21.881 --> 00:53:23.340
I'll be right back.


00:53:26.195 --> 00:53:29.355
- Alice, what did you see?
- The decision's been made.


00:53:29.355 --> 00:53:32.726
- What's going on?
- You're not going to Seattle?


00:53:32.726 --> 00:53:34.744
No...


00:53:34.744 --> 00:53:36.438
They're coming here.


00:53:37.187 --> 00:53:40.718
- They'll be here in four days.
- This could turn into a blood bath.


00:53:41.090 --> 00:53:44.068
- Who's behind it?
- I didn't see anyone I recognize.


00:53:45.222 --> 00:53:47.331
Maybe one...


00:53:47.331 --> 00:53:51.012
I know his face.
He's local, Riley Biers.


00:53:51.531 --> 00:53:52.633
He didn't start this.


00:53:52.633 --> 00:53:55.081
Whoever did
is staying out of the action.


00:53:55.081 --> 00:53:57.438
They must be playing with
the blind spots in your vision.


00:53:57.438 --> 00:53:59.048
Either way,
the army is coming...


00:53:59.048 --> 00:54:01.345
and there aren't enough of us
to protect the town.


00:54:01.345 --> 00:54:04.061
Hold up!
What damn army?


00:54:04.061 --> 00:54:07.627
- Newborns. Our kind.
- What are they after?


00:54:07.627 --> 00:54:11.165
They were passing around
Bella's scent. A red blouse.


00:54:11.165 --> 00:54:13.291
They're after Bella?


00:54:13.291 --> 00:54:16.411
- What the hell does this mean?
- It means an ugly fight.


00:54:16.411 --> 00:54:18.633
With lives lost.


00:54:22.833 --> 00:54:24.537
Alright...


00:54:24.537 --> 00:54:27.041
- We're in.
- No.


00:54:27.041 --> 00:54:29.134
You'll get yourselves killed,
noway.


00:54:29.134 --> 00:54:33.654
- I wasn't asking for permission.
- Edward.


00:54:37.003 --> 00:54:39.289
It means
more protection for you.


00:54:39.904 --> 00:54:45.004
Jacob. Do you believe Sam
will agree to... an understanding?


00:54:46.320 --> 00:54:49.080
As long as we get to kill
some vampires.


00:54:49.080 --> 00:54:53.475
- Jasper?
- They'll give us the numbers.


00:54:53.475 --> 00:54:56.118
And the newborns won't know
they even exist.


00:54:56.118 --> 00:54:58.834
- That'll give us an edge.
- We'll need to coordinate.


00:54:58.834 --> 00:55:02.904
- Carlisle, they'll gonna get hurt.
- We'll all need some training.


00:55:02.904 --> 00:55:05.931
Fighting newborns requires
knowledge that Jasper has.


00:55:05.931 --> 00:55:07.785
You're welcome to join us.


00:55:09.328 --> 00:55:12.557
Alright.
Name the time and place.


00:55:12.557 --> 00:55:14.179
Jake...


00:55:14.179 --> 00:55:16.940
You don't know
what you're getting yourself in to.


00:55:17.878 --> 00:55:19.855
Bella...


00:55:19.855 --> 00:55:24.126
This is what we do.
You should be happy.


00:55:24.126 --> 00:55:27.195
Look at us, working together.


00:55:27.195 --> 00:55:30.506
You're the one who wanted us
to get along, remember?


00:55:40.379 --> 00:55:41.831
Again!


00:55:54.699 --> 00:55:56.831
It's a graduation present.


00:56:16.027 --> 00:56:18.804
They don't trust us enough
to be in their human forms.


00:56:18.804 --> 00:56:21.312
They came.
That's what matters.


00:56:22.258 --> 00:56:24.182
Will you translate?


00:56:29.190 --> 00:56:30.955
Hey, Jake.


00:56:36.510 --> 00:56:38.266
Welcome.


00:56:40.108 --> 00:56:42.660
Jasper has experience
with newborns.


00:56:42.660 --> 00:56:44.853
He'll teach us
how to defeat them.


00:56:47.304 --> 00:56:49.346
They want to know
how the "newborns" is differ from us.


00:56:50.472 --> 00:56:52.098
They're a great deal
stronger than us,


00:56:52.098 --> 00:56:55.062
because their own human blood
lingers in their tissues.


00:56:55.755 --> 00:56:59.516
Our kind is never more
physically powerful...


00:56:59.516 --> 00:57:02.097
than in our first several months
of this life.


00:57:05.217 --> 00:57:07.381
Carlisle's right.


00:57:07.381 --> 00:57:09.739
That's why
they are created.


00:57:10.324 --> 00:57:14.221
A newborn army, doesn't need
thousands like a human army.


00:57:14.944 --> 00:57:17.321
And no human army
could stand against them.


00:57:19.191 --> 00:57:22.270
The two most important things
to remember are, first...


00:57:22.270 --> 00:57:23.933
Never let them
get their arms around you.


00:57:23.933 --> 00:57:27.069
They'll crush you instantly.
The second...


00:57:28.642 --> 00:57:31.458
Never go
for the obvious kill.


00:57:32.924 --> 00:57:38.024
They'll be expecting that.
And you will lose.


00:57:39.564 --> 00:57:41.277
Emmett?


00:57:47.981 --> 00:57:51.359
Don't hold back.
Not in my nature.


00:58:05.651 --> 00:58:07.210
Never lose focus.


00:58:28.317 --> 00:58:29.631
One more thing...


00:58:30.529 --> 00:58:33.140
Never turn your back
on your enemy.


00:59:20.269 --> 00:59:22.048
Some of you,
are gonna get hurt.


00:59:25.369 --> 00:59:29.169
Some of you
could get killed, because of me.


00:59:31.807 --> 00:59:34.264
It's gonna be a hundred times
worse than this, right?


00:59:57.358 --> 00:59:59.394
We're done for the day.


01:00:11.957 --> 01:00:13.983
Jasper...


01:00:16.475 --> 01:00:19.408
Are you sure, there's nothing
I can do to help?


01:00:19.408 --> 01:00:23.035
Your presence alone,
your scent will distract the newborns.


01:00:23.035 --> 01:00:27.443
Their hunting instinct will take over,
drive them crazy.


01:00:28.564 --> 01:00:30.697
Good. I'm glad.


01:00:32.788 --> 01:00:34.374
Hey.


01:00:34.374 --> 01:00:36.528
How do you know so much
about this?


01:00:38.050 --> 01:00:42.507
I didn't have quite the same upbringing
as my adopted siblings.


01:00:48.440 --> 01:00:50.068
Those bites are like mine.


01:00:50.911 --> 01:00:52.463
Battle scars.


01:00:54.013 --> 01:00:56.745
All the training the Confederate Army
gave me...


01:00:56.745 --> 01:00:59.042
was useless against
the newborns.


01:01:00.102 --> 01:01:04.049
Still,
I never lost a fight.


01:01:08.878 --> 01:01:11.850
This has happened
during the civil war?


01:01:11.850 --> 01:01:14.701
I was the youngest major
in the Texas cavalry.


01:01:14.701 --> 01:01:17.546
All without having seen
any real battle.


01:01:17.546 --> 01:01:18.761
Until...


01:01:20.554 --> 01:01:22.912
Until I'm not a certain immortal.


01:01:23.530 --> 01:01:25.363
Maria.


01:01:29.762 --> 01:01:30.972
<i>I was riding back
to Galveston...</i>


01:01:30.972 --> 01:01:34.490
<i>after evacuating
a column of women and children.</i>


01:01:34.490 --> 01:01:35.881
When I saw her...


01:01:37.029 --> 01:01:39.183
I immediately offered her my aid.


01:01:46.859 --> 01:01:50.045
Lovely. And an officer.


01:01:57.009 --> 01:02:02.209
You'd better do it, Maria.
I can never stop once I've started.


01:02:05.008 --> 01:02:09.791
- What's your name, soldier?
- Major Jasper Whitlock, Ma'am.


01:02:09.791 --> 01:02:11.540
I hope you survive.


01:02:12.660 --> 01:02:16.019
You maybe of
a great use to me.


01:02:20.883 --> 01:02:22.911
Maria was creating an army?


01:02:22.911 --> 01:02:25.050
They were very common
in the South.


01:02:25.050 --> 01:02:28.758
And cost a brutal battles
for territory.


01:02:28.758 --> 01:02:30.792
Maria won them all.


01:02:31.646 --> 01:02:36.646
She was smart, careful.
And she had me.


01:02:39.093 --> 01:02:41.938
<i>I was the second in command.</i>


01:02:41.938 --> 01:02:45.783
<i>My abilities to control emotions
served her well.</i>


01:02:46.683 --> 01:02:48.691
<i>I trained her newborns.</i>


01:02:51.747 --> 01:02:56.161
<i>An endless occupation since she never
let them live beyond their first year.</i>


01:02:59.160 --> 01:03:01.580
<i>It was my job
to dispose of them.</i>


01:03:22.156 --> 01:03:25.031
<i>I could feel
everything they felt.</i>


01:03:37.617 --> 01:03:40.339
I thought what Maria and I had
was love.


01:03:41.727 --> 01:03:46.427
But I was her puppet.
She pulled the strings.


01:03:47.594 --> 01:03:50.052
I didn't know
there was another way...


01:03:51.938 --> 01:03:53.976
Until I found Alice.


01:03:55.476 --> 01:03:58.486
Now she'd seen me coming,
of course.


01:03:58.486 --> 01:04:00.870
Kept me waiting long enough.


01:04:04.428 --> 01:04:06.401
My apologies, Ma'am.


01:04:08.057 --> 01:04:10.144
I don't know what I'd have become
without her.


01:04:12.916 --> 01:04:15.398
You'll never have to be
that again.


01:05:04.413 --> 01:05:05.490
What is it?


01:05:09.168 --> 01:05:12.270
The intruder...


01:05:12.270 --> 01:05:14.565
The newborn army.


01:05:16.188 --> 01:05:18.669
They're all her puppets.


01:05:20.620 --> 01:05:22.081
Victoria.


01:05:23.171 --> 01:05:26.457
Alice would've seen
if she wanted to make an army.


01:05:26.457 --> 01:05:29.633
Unless she's hiding
behind them,


01:05:29.633 --> 01:05:31.917
and she's letting
someone else decide.


01:06:00.475 --> 01:06:02.726
Welcome to the army.


01:06:11.902 --> 01:06:12.759
I'm not just gonna hide,


01:06:12.759 --> 01:06:14.759
while you're taking
all the risks for me?


01:06:16.414 --> 01:06:17.275
If it's Victoria involved...


01:06:17.275 --> 01:06:19.824
I need to keep you as far away
from the fight as possible.


01:06:19.824 --> 01:06:22.124
Jasper said that
I could be of help.


01:06:22.124 --> 01:06:23.483
We won't need your help.


01:06:23.483 --> 01:06:26.275
With the wolves in this,
it's an easy win.


01:06:26.275 --> 01:06:28.441
The rest of us,
aren't gonna have enough to do.


01:06:29.064 --> 01:06:31.291
Okay, either it's so dangerous
that I have to hide...


01:06:31.291 --> 01:06:33.420
Or it's so easy, that you're gonna be
side blind, which is it?


01:06:33.420 --> 01:06:36.097
It's dangerous for you.
It's easy for us.


01:06:37.936 --> 01:06:40.205
I think it's dangerous
for us to be apart.


01:06:41.035 --> 01:06:43.028
How many times
we have to prove that?


01:06:43.703 --> 01:06:47.153
I'll be worrying.
You'll be worried.


01:06:47.153 --> 01:06:49.427
And we''ll both
feel more horrible.


01:06:51.206 --> 01:06:52.292
Okay, you're right.


01:06:53.696 --> 01:06:55.067
So, I'm coming with you.


01:06:55.067 --> 01:06:57.011
No, we've got
to stay away together.


01:06:57.784 --> 01:07:00.691
I can't make you choose
between me and your family, it's...


01:07:00.691 --> 01:07:03.344
The only way I can protect you,
is to be with you.


01:07:07.881 --> 01:07:09.722
You're not fighting?


01:07:09.722 --> 01:07:11.877
What, you pull a muscle
or something?


01:07:11.877 --> 01:07:14.838
- He's doing it for me. Okay?
- Whatever.


01:07:15.657 --> 01:07:17.053
Just tell me the plan.


01:07:17.795 --> 01:07:20.070
This field will give us
an advantage in battle.


01:07:20.070 --> 01:07:22.600
We need to lure the newborns
with Bella's scent.


01:07:23.460 --> 01:07:25.163
It needs to end here.


01:07:25.163 --> 01:07:26.829
Edward and I
are going on a campsite.


01:07:26.829 --> 01:07:29.780
Even if he carries me,
they'll still pick up our scents.


01:07:30.211 --> 01:07:32.333
Your stench, however,
is revolting.


01:07:32.333 --> 01:07:34.507
Dude, you really don't want
to start comparing stinks.


01:07:34.507 --> 01:07:39.058
What he means, is that your scent
will mask mine if you carry me.


01:07:39.058 --> 01:07:40.532
Done.


01:07:40.532 --> 01:07:42.095
This is not a good idea.


01:07:42.095 --> 01:07:43.273
Edward.


01:07:43.273 --> 01:07:47.479
They won't want to get
anywhere near his... odor.


01:07:47.479 --> 01:07:49.243
Okay, let's just try it.


01:07:52.243 --> 01:07:55.113
- Eau de wolf, comin' up.
- Run.


01:08:04.795 --> 01:08:07.667
You gonna ask me
to sit out the fight, too?


01:08:07.667 --> 01:08:10.104
Or don't you care
about my safety?


01:08:10.104 --> 01:08:13.445
Of course I care,
but you'd say no.


01:08:14.038 --> 01:08:15.802
So I won't have a choice
anyways.


01:08:16.736 --> 01:08:19.447
Since I let Sam be alpha male.


01:08:19.447 --> 01:08:21.656
I got to live with the shots
he calls.


01:08:22.254 --> 01:08:24.469
Since you let Sam be alpha?


01:08:25.470 --> 01:08:29.570
I didn't want to be in a pack,
let alone be it's their leader.


01:08:31.226 --> 01:08:32.666
Wow.


01:08:33.750 --> 01:08:37.740
- Chief Jacob.
- Opted out.


01:08:37.740 --> 01:08:40.699
But every choice has
it's consequences.


01:08:40.699 --> 01:08:43.723
- Some more than others.
- Don't start.


01:08:43.723 --> 01:08:46.658
Everybody makes choices,
you gonna have to accept mine.


01:08:46.658 --> 01:08:49.357
You can love more than
one person at a time.


01:08:50.203 --> 01:08:53.960
I've seen it,
with Sam, Emily, and Leah.


01:08:55.359 --> 01:08:56.443
Well...


01:08:56.443 --> 01:09:00.722
- I'm not a wolf, I can't imprint.
- It has nothing to do with imprinting.


01:09:01.403 --> 01:09:05.179
It has to do with...
Feeling something for somebody.


01:09:05.719 --> 01:09:08.556
And I know
you feel something for me.


01:09:09.569 --> 01:09:11.834
I can sense
how I make you feel...


01:09:11.834 --> 01:09:13.460
Physically.


01:09:14.598 --> 01:09:16.429
I make you nervous.


01:09:20.757 --> 01:09:22.197
Jake.


01:09:24.000 --> 01:09:25.248
Don't worry.


01:09:26.356 --> 01:09:28.975
I promised I wouldn't kiss you
again until you asked.


01:09:30.310 --> 01:09:33.280
You're going to be keeping
that promise for a while, Chief.


01:09:36.979 --> 01:09:41.065
All I picked up was wolf stench.
No Bella.


01:09:43.700 --> 01:09:46.968
- This will work.
- Great.


01:09:56.651 --> 01:09:58.903
- Okay, Alice. Don't be a stranger.
- Okay.


01:10:01.238 --> 01:10:03.378
Your alibi for the battle
is all arranged.


01:10:03.378 --> 01:10:04.672
Really?


01:10:04.672 --> 01:10:07.367
I told your father that our whole
family's going camping this weekend.


01:10:07.367 --> 01:10:10.313
So you and I are having
a sleep over at my house.


01:10:11.129 --> 01:10:13.690
- Charlie is going fishing anyway.
- Charlie?


01:10:14.670 --> 01:10:16.837
You guys run
for the same basis now?


01:10:16.837 --> 01:10:18.677
Me, he likes.


01:10:19.663 --> 01:10:22.664
Actually, you and Edward will have
the house to yourself tonight.


01:10:26.406 --> 01:10:28.216
Like alone?


01:10:28.216 --> 01:10:31.778
We're all going hunting,
powering up for the battle.


01:10:34.372 --> 01:10:36.005
You're welcome.


01:10:37.725 --> 01:10:41.999
- Hey. Do you want a sandwich?
- No, I'm good.


01:10:43.508 --> 01:10:46.597
Well, the sister...
I like.


01:10:46.597 --> 01:10:50.145
Alice.
Yeah, she's great.


01:10:57.395 --> 01:10:59.799
Hey, Dad.
I was wondering...


01:11:00.932 --> 01:11:04.447
Why didn't you get remarried,
after Mom?


01:11:08.516 --> 01:11:09.867
I don't know...


01:11:11.356 --> 01:11:13.785
Guess I still haven't met
the right gal.


01:11:15.713 --> 01:11:18.335
- Why?
- I don't know.


01:11:21.149 --> 01:11:22.840
I thought you just...


01:11:22.840 --> 01:11:25.227
Maybe you gave up
on the whole institution of it.


01:11:26.227 --> 01:11:27.889
Of marriage.


01:11:29.301 --> 01:11:31.460
But do you think
there's any value in it?


01:11:33.337 --> 01:11:35.318
Yeah.


01:11:35.318 --> 01:11:36.874
Yeah, marriage has value.


01:11:38.513 --> 01:11:42.713
When you're older.
Much older.


01:11:44.678 --> 01:11:46.530
Like you're mother...


01:11:46.530 --> 01:11:48.921
It seem to work out fine for her
the second time round.


01:11:48.921 --> 01:11:52.283
- Later in life.
- Yeah, I guess.


01:11:54.350 --> 01:11:55.615
I mean...


01:11:55.615 --> 01:11:57.391
You definitely don't wanna
have to get married,


01:11:57.391 --> 01:12:00.963
because you weren't...
careful.


01:12:03.140 --> 01:12:04.506
What?


01:12:05.082 --> 01:12:06.295
Look, you know
what I'm talking about.


01:12:06.295 --> 01:12:08.053
There's...


01:12:08.053 --> 01:12:09.690
Things, that you need
to think about it, if you...


01:12:09.690 --> 01:12:11.302
If you gonna be...
physically intimate.


01:12:11.302 --> 01:12:13.855
Okay. Don't...
until we've enough of "The Talk".


01:12:13.855 --> 01:12:15.815
- Don't you just quit.
- It's just as embarrassing for me,


01:12:15.815 --> 01:12:17.998
- as it is for you.
- I doubt that.


01:12:17.998 --> 01:12:20.513
And don't bother, 'cause Mom
beat you too early ten years ago.


01:12:20.513 --> 01:12:22.473
Well, you didn't have a boyfriend
ten years ago.


01:12:22.473 --> 01:12:25.607
I'm sure things work
the same way.


01:12:27.408 --> 01:12:29.544
Alright.
So...


01:12:30.808 --> 01:12:33.327
You guys are...
taking precautions, and...


01:12:33.327 --> 01:12:36.946
Okay, dad. Please just
don't worry about that.


01:12:37.424 --> 01:12:41.083
Edward is... old school.


01:12:42.850 --> 01:12:44.953
Old school, great.


01:12:44.953 --> 01:12:46.438
What's that?
Like a code for something?


01:12:46.438 --> 01:12:48.311
Oh my god.
Dad...


01:12:48.311 --> 01:12:50.097
I'm a virgin!


01:12:50.097 --> 01:12:52.789
Okay, go.
Glad we covered that.


01:12:52.789 --> 01:12:54.537
Me too.


01:12:58.147 --> 01:12:59.803
Virgin...


01:13:01.139 --> 01:13:03.505
Liking Edward
a little bit more now.


01:13:14.391 --> 01:13:16.695
What are you doing here outside?
What's wrong?


01:13:17.831 --> 01:13:19.366
Nothing.


01:13:38.891 --> 01:13:41.431
It seems the only fair,
that I'd be represented as well.


01:13:46.339 --> 01:13:48.263
It's really pretty.


01:13:49.466 --> 01:13:50.957
Thanks.


01:13:58.721 --> 01:14:00.080
There's a bed.


01:14:01.615 --> 01:14:03.468
I thought you might need one
to sleep in.


01:14:06.639 --> 01:14:08.805
I think an air mattress
would've sufficed.


01:14:09.282 --> 01:14:12.580
- It is too much?
- No.


01:14:13.408 --> 01:14:14.936
No, it's perfect.


01:14:16.637 --> 01:14:18.441
I want to ask you something.


01:14:19.437 --> 01:14:20.912
Anything.


01:14:24.276 --> 01:14:26.539
Okay, marriage
is the condition for you,


01:14:26.539 --> 01:14:28.524
to change me yourself, right?


01:14:30.529 --> 01:14:32.278
Yes.


01:14:34.555 --> 01:14:38.146
Okay. I want to negotiate my
own condition.


01:14:39.774 --> 01:14:42.485
Anything you want,
It's yours.


01:14:43.981 --> 01:14:45.693
Do you promise?


01:14:47.132 --> 01:14:48.620
Yeah.


01:15:09.979 --> 01:15:11.419
Bella... no.


01:15:14.053 --> 01:15:16.187
You've said that you wanted me
to have every human experience.


01:15:16.187 --> 01:15:18.545
Not the ones
that support risk killing you.


01:15:18.545 --> 01:15:20.134
You won't.


01:15:21.493 --> 01:15:22.835
And everyone says,
once I'm changed...


01:15:22.835 --> 01:15:25.276
all I'm gonna want is
to slaughter the whole town.


01:15:25.759 --> 01:15:27.996
That part doesn't last forever.


01:15:28.363 --> 01:15:30.004
I want you.


01:15:31.296 --> 01:15:36.336
While I'm still me.
While I still want you this way.


01:15:40.318 --> 01:15:42.183
It's too dangerous.


01:15:42.862 --> 01:15:46.617
Try...
Just try.


01:15:48.230 --> 01:15:50.058
I'll go to some ridiculously
expensive college


01:15:50.058 --> 01:15:51.837
and let you buy me a car.


01:15:52.715 --> 01:15:55.355
I'll marry you, just try.


01:16:36.137 --> 01:16:38.782
Stop trying to take
your clothes off.


01:16:38.782 --> 01:16:41.345
- Do you want to do that part?
- Not tonight.


01:17:05.672 --> 01:17:08.555
Okay.
I mean, you don't...


01:17:10.520 --> 01:17:12.355
But, fine.


01:17:15.041 --> 01:17:17.873
Believe me, I want to.


01:17:19.591 --> 01:17:21.935
I just want to be married
to you first.


01:17:24.524 --> 01:17:28.130
You really make me feel like
I'm some sort of like a villain trying...


01:17:28.130 --> 01:17:30.578
steal your virtue
or something.


01:17:32.458 --> 01:17:35.000
It's not my virtue
I'm concerned about.


01:17:36.989 --> 01:17:39.120
Are you kidding?


01:17:39.120 --> 01:17:43.820
It's just one rule,
I wanna leave unbroken.


01:17:45.548 --> 01:17:49.067
It might be too late for my soul,
but I will protect yours.


01:17:50.457 --> 01:17:55.136
- I know it's not a modern notion.
- It's not modern.


01:17:55.136 --> 01:17:57.232
It's ancient.


01:17:59.346 --> 01:18:01.381
I'm from a different era.


01:18:03.777 --> 01:18:08.168
Things were...
a lot less complicated.


01:18:09.721 --> 01:18:14.721
And if I met you back then,
I would've courted to you.


01:18:16.397 --> 01:18:18.682
We'd have taken
chaperoned strolls,


01:18:18.682 --> 01:18:22.040
or had iced tea
on the porch.


01:18:32.473 --> 01:18:34.817
I may have stolen
a kiss or two.


01:18:35.709 --> 01:18:38.904
But, only...


01:18:38.904 --> 01:18:41.500
after asking
your father's permission.


01:18:43.116 --> 01:18:45.164
I would've got down
on one knee.


01:18:51.655 --> 01:18:53.962
And I would
presented you with a ring.


01:19:01.678 --> 01:19:03.152
This was my mother's.


01:19:07.032 --> 01:19:11.832
Isabella Swan. I promise
to love you, every moment forever.


01:19:13.048 --> 01:19:16.897
And would you do me the extraordinary
honor of marrying me?


01:19:22.692 --> 01:19:23.692
Yes.


01:19:45.903 --> 01:19:47.861
You're not coming with us?


01:19:56.410 --> 01:19:59.141
It will be a last minute decision.


01:20:00.870 --> 01:20:03.350
I told you how it works.


01:20:03.350 --> 01:20:06.936
The Cullens have powers.


01:20:07.531 --> 01:20:10.593
Don't underestimate them,
Riley.


01:20:10.593 --> 01:20:12.967
You'll have the numbers,


01:20:12.967 --> 01:20:15.178
but they'll be able to...


01:20:15.178 --> 01:20:19.084
anticipate your every move.


01:20:19.680 --> 01:20:22.970
- According to your friend.
- Yes.


01:20:22.970 --> 01:20:26.538
My dead friend.


01:20:28.697 --> 01:20:31.988
Laurent found out about
the things they could do,


01:20:33.987 --> 01:20:35.836
and they killed him.


01:20:37.619 --> 01:20:40.818
But not before he told me.


01:20:45.054 --> 01:20:46.916
Maybe he was wrong.


01:20:49.858 --> 01:20:51.712
I mean...


01:20:51.712 --> 01:20:54.296
This is supposed to be...


01:20:54.296 --> 01:20:57.331
Cullen territory.


01:20:57.331 --> 01:21:01.730
But we've been tearing it up
and I've never even seen them here.


01:21:02.417 --> 01:21:04.593
You don't trust me.


01:21:05.445 --> 01:21:07.906
With my life.
I'm just saying that...


01:21:07.906 --> 01:21:11.644
I'm doing this for us.
So that we can feed,


01:21:12.067 --> 01:21:17.167
without their retaliation.
I can't live in fear anymore,


01:21:17.167 --> 01:21:18.822
waiting for them to attack.


01:21:18.822 --> 01:21:21.847
I won't let them.


01:21:21.847 --> 01:21:26.847
I'm going to
end the Cullen clan.


01:21:29.346 --> 01:21:31.218
I swear.


01:21:48.088 --> 01:21:52.081
I love you. So much.


01:22:12.059 --> 01:22:13.442
You're going overboard.


01:22:14.130 --> 01:22:16.743
If this is all I can contribute,
I want to be thorough.


01:22:16.743 --> 01:22:18.794
The newborns will be frantic.


01:22:21.203 --> 01:22:24.084
It's Okay. Don't make yourself
uncomfortable.


01:22:24.685 --> 01:22:26.572
It doesn't bother me anymore.


01:22:28.202 --> 01:22:29.709
Since when?


01:22:29.709 --> 01:22:32.472
Since I spent 24 hours
thinking you were dead.


01:22:34.347 --> 01:22:35.959
You're not wearing your ring.


01:22:38.221 --> 01:22:40.161
Well, I didn't want to risk
losing it.


01:22:42.478 --> 01:22:44.479
Or risk Jacob seeing it?


01:22:47.176 --> 01:22:50.896
I think we should wait to tell him.
I mean, at least till after the fight.


01:22:50.896 --> 01:22:53.551
- If you're having second thoughts...
- I'm not.


01:22:53.777 --> 01:22:56.537
I just want him to have
a clear head.


01:22:56.537 --> 01:22:58.124
Whose head is unclear?


01:22:59.462 --> 01:23:01.115
Nobody's, I hope.


01:23:02.183 --> 01:23:04.155
Alice says
there's a storm coming.


01:23:04.155 --> 01:23:07.872
Yeah, I can feel it.
We should get going.


01:23:09.197 --> 01:23:10.878
I'll see you
in a couple of hours.


01:23:20.983 --> 01:23:22.468
Something up?


01:23:25.300 --> 01:23:27.074
A bunch of vampires
trying to kill me.


01:23:27.870 --> 01:23:29.870
Same old, same old.


01:24:47.231 --> 01:24:48.551
Thank you.


01:24:50.949 --> 01:24:52.878
You should get back
before the storm hits.


01:24:52.878 --> 01:24:54.697
No, I'm staying.


01:24:54.697 --> 01:24:55.870
You'll need my connection
to the pack,


01:24:55.870 --> 01:24:57.469
to keep tabs
on what's going on.


01:24:57.469 --> 01:25:00.179
- You're not going to fight?
- Seth will spell me in the morning.


01:25:01.335 --> 01:25:03.195
He's not happy
about missing the action,


01:25:03.195 --> 01:25:05.005
but it'll keep him
out of trouble.


01:25:06.111 --> 01:25:07.857
Let's get you inside.


01:25:25.882 --> 01:25:28.060
I should have chosen
a site lower down.


01:25:28.060 --> 01:25:30.632
No, It's fine. I'm okay.


01:25:31.655 --> 01:25:32.897
What can I do?


01:25:45.934 --> 01:25:49.023
I can't sleep with all that
teeth chattering going on.


01:25:56.547 --> 01:25:57.709
Forget it.


01:25:58.991 --> 01:26:04.091
She may need her toes someday.
And let's face it...


01:26:04.091 --> 01:26:06.480
I'm hotter than you.


01:26:10.426 --> 01:26:13.756
Get your hand off me!


01:26:13.756 --> 01:26:16.053
Get your hands off her!


01:26:16.053 --> 01:26:17.788
Don't fight.


01:26:20.642 --> 01:26:23.047
She gets sick, it's on you.


01:26:39.466 --> 01:26:41.210
Why!
you're freezing, Bella


01:26:42.845 --> 01:26:46.472
Relax,
You'll warm up soon.


01:26:47.802 --> 01:26:49.868
Faster
if you took your clothes off.


01:26:50.659 --> 01:26:54.044
- Jake.
- Survival one oh one.


01:27:24.805 --> 01:27:28.222
Can you, at least attempt
to control your thoughts?


01:27:30.485 --> 01:27:33.850
I really get under that
ice cold skin of yours, don't I?


01:27:36.478 --> 01:27:38.642
What?


01:27:38.642 --> 01:27:40.930
Are you doubting her feelings
for you?


01:27:43.902 --> 01:27:45.899
Nice...


01:27:45.899 --> 01:27:48.767
So picking through
my brain's okay,


01:27:48.767 --> 01:27:51.947
but letting me into yours,
forget it.


01:27:55.545 --> 01:27:56.628
Look...


01:27:58.309 --> 01:28:01.194
- I know she's in love with you.
- Oh, good.


01:28:01.694 --> 01:28:03.989
But she's in love with me, too.


01:28:06.309 --> 01:28:08.596
She just won't admit it to herself.


01:28:11.848 --> 01:28:13.661
I can't tell you
if you're right.


01:28:15.743 --> 01:28:18.406
Then let me ask you something.


01:28:18.406 --> 01:28:21.352
- If she chooses me...
- She won't.


01:28:21.682 --> 01:28:23.334
If she did.


01:28:24.890 --> 01:28:26.784
Would you try to kill me?


01:28:27.753 --> 01:28:29.847
That's an intriguing idea.


01:28:34.743 --> 01:28:38.448
But no.
I couldn't hurt her like that.


01:28:38.967 --> 01:28:42.568
see, you'd just turn her into
a bloodsucking demon like you.


01:28:42.568 --> 01:28:46.086
I don't want that.
I never wanted that.


01:28:46.086 --> 01:28:48.538
- So stop her.
- I tried.


01:28:50.178 --> 01:28:53.134
- I left.
- But you gave up too quickly.


01:28:55.063 --> 01:28:58.651
If you'd stayed away
another six months,


01:28:58.651 --> 01:29:01.939
I could've made her happy.
Trust me.


01:29:03.392 --> 01:29:06.014
You have to consider...


01:29:06.014 --> 01:29:08.885
that I might be better for her
than you are.


01:29:10.763 --> 01:29:13.006
I have considered that.


01:29:16.659 --> 01:29:18.432
I know you can protect her.


01:29:21.323 --> 01:29:24.865
But you can give her a life,
a human life.


01:29:24.865 --> 01:29:26.834
It's all I want for her.


01:29:29.470 --> 01:29:31.282
But, I'm not...


01:29:31.282 --> 01:29:35.358
I'm not going to force her
into anything, ever again.


01:29:37.120 --> 01:29:40.306
The last time I tried,
it almost killed us both.


01:29:42.939 --> 01:29:45.449
Yeah, that I remember.


01:29:49.579 --> 01:29:51.694
When you thought
she was gone...


01:29:54.184 --> 01:29:56.386
that you'd lost her...


01:29:58.426 --> 01:30:01.948
How did you... cope?


01:30:03.484 --> 01:30:05.424
There're no words.


01:30:11.238 --> 01:30:13.797
But I wouldn't wash it
on anyone, Jacob.


01:30:16.333 --> 01:30:20.567
This might sound odd,
but I'm glad you're here.


01:30:20.567 --> 01:30:21.781
Pretty neat.


01:30:23.633 --> 01:30:26.941
As much as I'd love to kill you,
I'm glad she's warm.


01:30:29.892 --> 01:30:32.547
If we weren't
natural enemies...


01:30:32.547 --> 01:30:36.848
and you weren't trying to steal
my reason for existing...


01:30:36.848 --> 01:30:39.225
I might actually like you.


01:30:40.026 --> 01:30:41.504
Well...


01:30:42.830 --> 01:30:46.657
If you weren't planning on sucking
the life out of the girl I love,


01:30:47.969 --> 01:30:49.706
I might...


01:30:56.459 --> 01:31:00.069
No...
Not even then.


01:31:07.791 --> 01:31:11.489
But she could still
change her mind, you know.


01:31:17.896 --> 01:31:19.794
Then I'd let her go.


01:31:39.277 --> 01:31:40.768
Fine. Hi, Seth.


01:31:44.257 --> 01:31:46.006
Where's Jacob?
Did he already...


01:31:46.006 --> 01:31:47.276
Not yet.


01:31:48.926 --> 01:31:51.551
He's checking to see if the woods
are clear before he goes.


01:31:59.635 --> 01:32:02.065
I'm really sorry
about last night.


01:32:02.065 --> 01:32:03.698
I couldn't have been
easy on you.


01:32:03.698 --> 01:32:06.818
It definitely won't make my list
of top ten favorite evenings.


01:32:07.737 --> 01:32:09.376
You have a list?


01:32:10.224 --> 01:32:12.063
All ten I spent with you.


01:32:13.185 --> 01:32:15.421
Number one is when you said
you'd marry me.


01:32:16.833 --> 01:32:18.637
Mrs. Cullen.


01:32:21.540 --> 01:32:23.541
This is the twenty-first century,


01:32:23.541 --> 01:32:25.541
I always wanna
hyphenate my name.


01:32:26.211 --> 01:32:28.111
You're marrying him?


01:32:28.626 --> 01:32:30.067
Jake...


01:32:34.034 --> 01:32:35.723
You knew he was listening?


01:32:36.564 --> 01:32:38.414
He deserves to know.


01:32:38.958 --> 01:32:40.413
- Jake, stop!
- Bella, let him...


01:32:40.413 --> 01:32:41.133
Don't!


01:32:44.797 --> 01:32:46.500
Jake, stop!


01:32:49.661 --> 01:32:53.915
- Jake, please!
- I'm done! I'm so done!


01:32:54.484 --> 01:32:57.093
- What can I do?
- You can't do anything.


01:32:57.093 --> 01:32:59.827
I can. By going out there
and killing something.


01:32:59.827 --> 01:33:03.093
No! You're not thinking clearly,
don't do that!


01:33:03.093 --> 01:33:05.346
Maybe I'll get my self killed
and make it simple for you.


01:33:05.346 --> 01:33:08.941
No! Just, Jake...
Stay!


01:33:09.765 --> 01:33:11.356
Why?


01:33:12.841 --> 01:33:15.086
Give me one good reason.


01:33:15.803 --> 01:33:17.785
Because I don't wanna lose you.


01:33:19.304 --> 01:33:21.077
It's not good enough.


01:33:21.947 --> 01:33:24.144
Because you're too important.


01:33:27.392 --> 01:33:29.229
Still not good enough.


01:33:30.164 --> 01:33:31.739
Jacob!


01:33:35.047 --> 01:33:36.689
Kiss me!


01:33:39.640 --> 01:33:43.984
I'm asking you to kiss me.


01:34:30.813 --> 01:34:33.219
That should have been
our first kiss.


01:34:39.166 --> 01:34:41.066
I gotta go.


01:34:43.469 --> 01:34:45.483
I'll be back.


01:35:15.031 --> 01:35:16.669
You saw.


01:35:17.817 --> 01:35:21.842
No. But Jacob's thoughts
are very loud.


01:35:22.828 --> 01:35:24.398
I don't know what happened.


01:35:26.358 --> 01:35:27.784
You love him.


01:35:32.291 --> 01:35:33.921
I love you more.


01:35:35.748 --> 01:35:37.733
I know.


01:35:51.715 --> 01:35:53.376
It's starting.


01:36:53.360 --> 01:36:55.335
Jacob just got there.


01:37:01.091 --> 01:37:02.760
He's good.


01:38:01.394 --> 01:38:02.865
Someone's hurt?


01:38:03.813 --> 01:38:07.182
She's close.
I can hear her thoughts.


01:38:07.182 --> 01:38:09.049
Seth, go.


01:38:13.515 --> 01:38:16.144
She knew we weren't there,
but she caught my scent.


01:38:16.144 --> 01:38:17.959
She knew you'd be with me.


01:38:18.999 --> 01:38:20.699
She found us.


01:38:24.092 --> 01:38:25.991
She's not alone.


01:38:34.899 --> 01:38:38.174
Riley...
Listen to me.


01:38:39.030 --> 01:38:42.212
Victoria's just using you,
to distract me.


01:38:42.810 --> 01:38:44.614
But she knows I'll kill you.


01:38:48.001 --> 01:38:51.479
In fact, she'll be glad she doesn't
have to deal with you anymore.


01:38:52.375 --> 01:38:54.368
Don't listen, Riley.


01:38:54.670 --> 01:38:56.855
I told you
about their mind tricks.


01:38:56.855 --> 01:39:01.179
I can read her mind,
so I know what she thinks of you.


01:39:01.179 --> 01:39:02.917
He's lying.


01:39:02.917 --> 01:39:08.017
She only created you and this army
to avenge her true mate, James.


01:39:08.819 --> 01:39:12.727
It's the only thing
she cares about. Not you.


01:39:14.486 --> 01:39:18.666
There's only you.
You know that.


01:39:20.455 --> 01:39:22.872
Think about it.


01:39:22.872 --> 01:39:27.672
You're from Forks,
you know the area.


01:39:28.238 --> 01:39:30.565
That's the only reason
she chose you.


01:39:31.703 --> 01:39:33.529
She doesn't love you.


01:39:34.079 --> 01:39:36.298
Riley...


01:39:36.298 --> 01:39:39.818
Don't let him do this to us.


01:39:41.451 --> 01:39:43.973
You know I love you.


01:39:57.122 --> 01:39:58.931
You're dead.


01:40:13.277 --> 01:40:15.549
You won't get another chance
like this again.


01:40:19.951 --> 01:40:21.323
You want her!


01:40:23.154 --> 01:40:26.727
You want me to feel the pain
you felt when I killed James.


01:40:28.538 --> 01:40:31.602
When I tore him to pieces.


01:40:33.686 --> 01:40:37.160
When I turned him into ash.


01:40:38.606 --> 01:40:43.423
When I turned him
into nothing.


01:42:02.669 --> 01:42:04.999
Victoria!


01:42:04.999 --> 01:42:06.079
Victoria!


01:43:03.223 --> 01:43:07.041
- Something's wrong.
- Alice needs us to go.


01:43:07.041 --> 01:43:08.467
And now.


01:43:31.082 --> 01:43:34.126
- How long?
- A few minutes. Maybe ten.


01:43:34.126 --> 01:43:35.508
The pack needs to leave.


01:43:35.508 --> 01:43:38.176
The Volturi won't honor a truce
with the werewolves.


01:43:45.275 --> 01:43:46.725
Leah, don't!


01:44:03.599 --> 01:44:05.176
Jacob!


01:44:08.321 --> 01:44:11.092
Jacob. Hold on, Carlisle
is gonna take care of you.


01:44:11.092 --> 01:44:13.496
The bones on the right half
of his body are shattered.


01:44:15.090 --> 01:44:17.520
- Bella.
- Jake, I'm right here.


01:44:19.304 --> 01:44:21.773
- Jacob, you idiot. I had it.
- Leah.


01:44:21.773 --> 01:44:24.596
I need to set the bones before
his accelerated healing kicks in.


01:44:24.596 --> 01:44:26.857
- It's already starting.
- We need to get him out of here.


01:44:26.857 --> 01:44:29.019
We're not gonna win a fight
with the Volturi.


01:44:29.923 --> 01:44:32.796
- We'll take him back to Billy's.
- I'll be there as soon as I can.


01:44:33.266 --> 01:44:34.696
Hang in there, Jake.


01:44:46.462 --> 01:44:47.875
We got you.


01:44:48.762 --> 01:44:50.318
They're coming.


01:45:11.256 --> 01:45:12.664
Impressive.


01:45:12.664 --> 01:45:16.256
I've never seen a coven escape
an assault of this magnitude intact.


01:45:17.256 --> 01:45:18.842
We were lucky.


01:45:20.208 --> 01:45:21.896
I doubt that.


01:45:23.854 --> 01:45:26.668
It appears we missed
an entertaining fight.


01:45:26.668 --> 01:45:30.497
Yes. It's not often
we're rendered unnecessary.


01:45:30.497 --> 01:45:33.546
If you'd arrived a half hour ago,
you would've fulfilled your purpose.


01:45:35.099 --> 01:45:36.938
Pity.


01:45:40.050 --> 01:45:41.849
You missed one.


01:45:48.552 --> 01:45:51.386
We offered her asylum
in exchange for her surrender.


01:45:52.255 --> 01:45:54.151
That wasn't yours to offer.


01:45:57.362 --> 01:45:58.751
Why did you come?


01:46:04.713 --> 01:46:06.160
Who created you?


01:46:07.682 --> 01:46:08.814
You don't need to do that.


01:46:08.814 --> 01:46:11.182
She'll tell you
anything you want to know.


01:46:11.182 --> 01:46:12.589
I know.


01:46:14.760 --> 01:46:17.153
I don't know


01:46:17.153 --> 01:46:19.233
Riley wouldn't tell us.


01:46:19.233 --> 01:46:21.530
He said our thoughts
weren't safe.


01:46:21.530 --> 01:46:25.123
Her name was Victoria.
Perhaps you knew her.


01:46:25.756 --> 01:46:29.269
Edward. If the Volturi had
knowledge of Victoria,


01:46:29.269 --> 01:46:30.795
they would've stopped her.


01:46:31.766 --> 01:46:33.533
Isn't that right, Jane?


01:46:35.447 --> 01:46:37.139
Of course.


01:46:38.492 --> 01:46:39.977
Felix.


01:46:40.764 --> 01:46:42.731
She didn't know
what she was doing.


01:46:44.171 --> 01:46:46.666
We'll take responsibility for her.


01:46:47.320 --> 01:46:49.146
Give her a chance.


01:46:51.476 --> 01:46:54.337
The Volturi don't give
second chances.


01:46:55.752 --> 01:46:57.947
Keep that in mind.


01:46:57.947 --> 01:47:00.744
Caius will be interested to know
that she's still human.


01:47:01.281 --> 01:47:02.921
The date is set.


01:47:06.298 --> 01:47:08.185
Take care of that, Felix.


01:47:09.173 --> 01:47:10.947
I'd like to go home.


01:47:45.357 --> 01:47:49.012
- It's been going on for a while.
- Doc's rebreaking his bones.


01:47:49.012 --> 01:47:50.939
Why'd he have to butt in?
I could've taken that tick...


01:47:50.939 --> 01:47:52.908
Oh, give it a rest, Leah.


01:47:59.109 --> 01:48:01.256
The worst is over.
He'll be alright.


01:48:02.033 --> 01:48:03.104
I gave him some morphine,


01:48:03.104 --> 01:48:05.474
but his body temperature
will burn it off soon.


01:48:05.474 --> 01:48:07.408
I'll come back
to set up a drip.


01:48:08.312 --> 01:48:09.806
Thank you.


01:48:19.511 --> 01:48:21.419
He's asking for you.


01:48:35.784 --> 01:48:37.597
Hey, Jake.


01:48:40.500 --> 01:48:41.500
Hey.


01:48:54.493 --> 01:48:56.963
I was worried about you.


01:48:56.963 --> 01:48:58.954
You were worried about me?


01:49:00.205 --> 01:49:01.794
Yeah.


01:49:02.800 --> 01:49:05.541
I guessed Edward
would read my thoughts.


01:49:08.244 --> 01:49:10.393
Was he hard on you?


01:49:10.393 --> 01:49:14.387
He wasn't even mad at me.
Or you.


01:49:15.647 --> 01:49:17.447
Well, damn.


01:49:19.620 --> 01:49:21.560
He's better than I thought.


01:49:22.224 --> 01:49:24.244
He's not playing a game.


01:49:26.240 --> 01:49:27.570
Right.


01:49:31.026 --> 01:49:33.006
Bella...


01:49:35.705 --> 01:49:38.960
He's not as perfect
as you think.


01:49:41.925 --> 01:49:43.962
I know who he is.


01:49:48.067 --> 01:49:50.647
I must not talk about that.


01:49:51.644 --> 01:49:54.867
I'd rather get all the rebreaking
done at once.


01:50:00.790 --> 01:50:03.977
At least I know
I did everything I could.


01:50:07.480 --> 01:50:10.986
Wasn't easy making you
admit your feelings for me.


01:50:13.985 --> 01:50:17.307
I only fought them, because I know
they wouldn't change anything.


01:50:25.399 --> 01:50:28.497
I'm exactly right for you,
Bella.


01:50:30.854 --> 01:50:35.854
It would be as easy
as breathing with me.


01:50:41.514 --> 01:50:43.914
You know I love you.


01:50:50.609 --> 01:50:53.735
You know how much
I wish it was enough.


01:51:05.392 --> 01:51:06.847
Should I come back?


01:51:09.615 --> 01:51:12.049
I need some time.


01:51:16.069 --> 01:51:18.748
But I'll always be waiting.


01:51:23.193 --> 01:51:26.208
Untill my heart stops beating.


01:51:28.254 --> 01:51:30.638
Maybe even then.


01:51:52.686 --> 01:51:55.662
- August thirteenth?
- Yeah.


01:51:55.662 --> 01:51:57.659
it's a month
before my birthday.


01:51:57.659 --> 01:51:59.750
I don't need to be
another year older than you.


01:52:01.600 --> 01:52:03.660
Alice said she can get
the wedding together by then.


01:52:04.612 --> 01:52:06.308
I'm sure she can.


01:52:08.520 --> 01:52:10.205
There's no rush.


01:52:12.728 --> 01:52:16.939
I've chosen my life.
I want to start living it.


01:52:16.939 --> 01:52:20.260
And so, you're gonna let Alice
plan the whole thing?


01:52:20.807 --> 01:52:22.084
Yeah.


01:52:22.084 --> 01:52:25.165
Dress, the reception,
the guest list...


01:52:25.165 --> 01:52:27.888
I mean, who knows
who she's gonna invite?


01:52:30.073 --> 01:52:31.594
Does it matter?


01:52:36.164 --> 01:52:38.159
I just don't know
why you're doing this.


01:52:38.159 --> 01:52:40.885
What? The wedding?


01:52:44.537 --> 01:52:46.946
You're trying to make
everyone else happy.


01:52:48.117 --> 01:52:50.552
But you're already
giving away too much.


01:52:51.724 --> 01:52:53.210
You're wrong.


01:53:01.201 --> 01:53:04.757
This wasn't a choice
between you and Jacob.


01:53:08.297 --> 01:53:12.652
It was between who I should be
and who I am.


01:53:16.201 --> 01:53:18.228
I've always felt out of step.


01:53:19.171 --> 01:53:21.641
Like literally,
stumbling through my life.


01:53:24.224 --> 01:53:26.094
I'm never felt normal.


01:53:28.846 --> 01:53:30.908
Because I'm not normal.


01:53:32.070 --> 01:53:34.056
I don't wanna be.


01:53:35.107 --> 01:53:38.425
I've had to face death...


01:53:38.425 --> 01:53:42.401
and loss and pain,
in your world.


01:53:42.401 --> 01:53:45.491
But, I've also never felt
stronger...


01:53:48.391 --> 01:53:51.502
more real, more...
my self.


01:53:53.542 --> 01:53:55.662
Because it's my world, too.


01:53:59.026 --> 01:54:01.343
It's where I belong.


01:54:07.689 --> 01:54:10.208
So, it's not just about me.


01:54:11.988 --> 01:54:13.188
No, sorry.


01:54:17.433 --> 01:54:20.455
I've made a mess trying
to figure all this out, but...


01:54:21.516 --> 01:54:23.186
I wanna do it right.


01:54:23.853 --> 01:54:26.768
And I wanna tie my self
to you,


01:54:26.768 --> 01:54:29.328
in every way
humanly possible.


01:54:32.545 --> 01:54:34.568
Starting with a wedding.


01:54:38.490 --> 01:54:40.750
Actually...


01:54:40.750 --> 01:54:44.259
Something,
a little more difficult first.


01:54:44.259 --> 01:54:46.364
And maybe even dangerous.


01:54:51.474 --> 01:54:53.575
We have to tell Charlie.


01:54:57.039 --> 01:54:59.258
It's highly dangerous.


01:54:59.258 --> 01:55:01.437
It's a good thing
you're bulletproof.


01:55:03.642 --> 01:55:05.924
I'm gonna need that ring.

